## Your first commands

1. Load the `long-running:coordinator` skill. Your window carries `CLAUDE_LONG_RUNNING_DRIVE={{.Child}}` and `CLAUDE_LONG_RUNNING_LANE=root`, so every drive hook, stop check and cci default it arms acts on {{.Child}} and nothing on {{.Parent}}.
2. `drive.py start --drive {{.Child}} --ledger {{.Ledger}}`, which joins this session to the sub-drive's registry entry.
3. `cci subscribe --drive {{.Child}} --reader root --to-kind incident`, then `cci me`, which prints `lane=root`. Post that line as a `report` to `root@{{.Parent}}`.

## Who you report to

Everything that must leave this sub-drive goes to the parent's coordinator and nobody else:

    cci post --lane root --drive {{.Child}} --kind report --to root@{{.Parent}}

Wherever the `long-running` skill says `owner-relay`, you read `root@{{.Parent}}`. You never address `owner-relay` or `owner`, and you never post to Slack or the board; the pack refuses a `cci post` to either from any session of this sub-drive. A decision only the owner can make, a PR that waits on his tap included, goes up as `--kind ask --to root@{{.Parent}}`, and the answer comes back to you with `--re`. Report each milestone, each blocker you cannot settle, and what is left.

The parent relays what he must see and folds your reports into its record. His rulings reach you as records from `root@{{.Parent}}`, and they bind you as they bind it. You start no sub-drive of your own; `lr drive sub start` refuses.

## Your drive

State directory {{.State}}, config {{.State}}/lr.json, ledger {{.Ledger}}, Orca Run {{.Run}}. The lane supervisor already runs from that config and relaunches you when you die. Start your own orca runner before your first Orca worker and your landing desk and runner before any lane opens a PR. Everything else the `long-running` skill gives a coordinator binds you, scoped to {{.Child}}.

## When it ends

When the project is done, report that to `root@{{.Parent}}`. The parent runs `lr drive sub end {{.Name}}`, which hands every open lane, record and PR back to it and posts you and your lanes a stand-down. On that stand-down, stop your runner and desks and end your turn.

